# grantcheck configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is gitignored and
# must never be committed. Nothing in this file is required to run
# `uvx grantcheck --ein 12-3456789` — that works with an empty environment.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENGRANTS_API_KEY — OPTIONAL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adds a live layer on top of the report: when a readiness check comes back
# clean, grantcheck appends grant opportunities currently open to that
# organization, matched on EIN, NTEE code, and state.
#
# Where to get it: sign in at https://opengrants.io and create a key in the
# Developer Dashboard. API docs: https://ops.opengrants.io/api-docs
# Opportunity matching uses POST /match-grants-api, which is available on the
# Pro and Developer tiers. A key from a lower tier still works for the rest of
# the API; the matching section is simply omitted.
#
# Without this key grantcheck runs every readiness check and prints the full
# report. A missing, invalid, expired, or rate-limited key degrades silently —
# it will never break or delay the core command.
OPENGRANTS_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAM_API_KEY — OPTIONAL for the CLI, REQUIRED for the data ingest job
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An api.data.gov key for the SAM.gov Entity Management API.
#
# Where to get it: https://api.data.gov/signup/ — free, instant, email only.
# API docs: https://open.gsa.gov/api/entity-api/
#
# For the CLI this is OPTIONAL. Without it, SAM.gov registration status,
# expiration date, and UEI are read from the daily public snapshot bundled into
# the grantcheck index, and the report labels them with the snapshot date. With
# it, those three checks are performed live against SAM.gov and labelled as of
# the moment you ran the command. If you are inside two weeks of a deadline,
# set the key.
#
# For the ingest job that builds and publishes the grantcheck index, and for
# the hosted companion at check.opengrants.io, this is REQUIRED.
#
# Only public-tier entity data is ever requested. Do not use a key with
# sensitive-tier ("FOUO") entitlements with this tool.
SAM_API_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GRANTCHECK_INDEX_BASE_URL — OPTIONAL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Override the location grantcheck fetches its prebuilt data index from. Set
# this to run against a mirror, an internal cache, or a locally built index in
# an air-gapped environment. Defaults to the public index; the GitHub release
# assets on egeria-corporation/grantcheck are the fallback mirror.
# GRANTCHECK_INDEX_BASE_URL=https://index.opengrants.io/grantcheck

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GRANTCHECK_CACHE_DIR — OPTIONAL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where downloaded index shards are cached. Defaults to the platform user cache
# directory (on Linux, ~/.cache/grantcheck). Set it if you want the cache on a
# shared volume or somewhere with more room.
# GRANTCHECK_CACHE_DIR=
